      <div class="mt-16">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">Common Mistakes Buyers Make</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Under $1,000 the compromises are real, and the mistake is usually accepting the wrong one rather than accepting any at all.</p>
        <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
          <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Expecting a running treadmill at a walking price</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Budget motors and decks handle walking and light jogging honestly. Sustained running is where the money you saved reappears as noise, heat, and wear.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Being sold by peak horsepower</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Peak figures are marketing numbers at this price point. Compare continuous-duty ratings only, or the flimsiest machine on the shelf will read as the strongest.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying at the stated weight capacity</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Budget frames are least forgiving at their limits. Leave a real buffer rather than buying to the number on the box.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring the warranty terms</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Cheap machines vary enormously in parts and labour coverage. A slightly pricier treadmill with a longer motor warranty is often the cheaper machine over five years.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
